    <string name="alpha_about">About UNYRI</string>
    <string name="alpha_agreement">User agreement</string>
    <string name="alpha_accept">I accept the alpha test agreement</string>
    <string name="alpha_terms_version">Alpha test · 13 September 2026</string>
    <string name="alpha_description">UNYRI is a messenger for conversations, photos, files, voice messages and audio/video calls. Connect to your own server on a computer or a hosted server, or choose a server operated by someone you trust.</string>
    <string name="alpha_warning">This is an alpha test. Features may change and errors or data loss are possible. Keep important files separately.</string>
    <string name="alpha_server_description">Choose a server and operator you trust. The operator controls access and can see account data, connection metadata and reports you send. End-to-end encryption protects private message content, but does not guarantee an honest operator or server availability. Conversation participants must use the same server.</string>
    <string name="alpha_terms_1">1. These terms cover voluntary testing of the UNYRI alpha application. You may stop testing at any time. This test does not create a paid subscription or promise a hosted server.</string>
    <string name="alpha_terms_2">2. The application and the selected server may have different operators. You choose your server and are responsible for checking its operator, rules and contact details. A self-hosted server runs on its operator’s infrastructure; the UNYRI developer does not automatically receive its user data or reports.</string>
    <string name="alpha_terms_3">3. Private messages use end-to-end encryption. Account information, connection metadata and call signalling are not all hidden from the server. Protect your device and credentials, verify identity-key changes and use HTTPS. Lost encryption keys can make old history unavailable.</string>
    <string name="alpha_terms_4">4. A problem report is sent only after your confirmation. Its description, selected screenshots, account identifier and app/OS versions are readable by the operator of the selected server. Remove passwords and private details before sending. The standard UNYRI server removes reports older than 30 days during its hourly cleanup; ask your operator about custom settings and backups. Optional automatic diagnostics are configured separately.</string>
    <string name="alpha_terms_5">5. Respect other people and applicable law. Do not use UNYRI for unlawful content, harassment, spam or attempts to compromise other accounts or servers. The selected server may have additional rules. Contact its operator about account access and reports.</string>
    <string name="alpha_terms_6">6. Alpha features and availability are not guaranteed. Do not rely on UNYRI for emergency communication or as the only copy of important data. These testing terms do not exclude rights that cannot lawfully be waived. Store publication and commercial licensing require separate finalized publisher and privacy information.</string>
    <string name="server_edit_help">Enter an HTTPS server address. This alpha build can also use HTTP on a trusted local network. Sign out before changing servers.</string>
    <string name="server_edit_failed">Could not save the address. Check the scheme and host; paths, passwords and query parameters are not allowed.</string>
    <string name="server_signout_warning">Changing servers requires signing out. Local account data and pending messages will be cleared. Preserve important history and finish pending sends first.</string>
